{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>For</b> [is] <b>Eloheinu</b> — from afar, or 'Eloheinu' is its reading." "<b>And the flock of His hand</b> — corresponding to 'His hands formed [us].'" "And the meaning of <b>today</b> — it is joined with 'come let us bow down': if in your hearts you would hear His voice, bow down to Him today. 'If you will hear His voice' — and this is the voice of HaShem."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 95, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:37:20.931132511Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}